    "wizard": {
        "fields": []
    },
    "notes": {
        "22222222-de30-4000-8000-000000000002": {
            "content": "## How to verify this trigger (storefront)\n\nOne-time setup: in Settings → Customer accounts switch to the new customer accounts and enable **Self-serve returns**; in Settings → Payments activate the **(for testing) Bogus Gateway**.\n\n1. Start this flow.\n2. Open the online store (https://<store>.myshopify.com; the password of a dev store is in Online Store → Preferences).\n3. Add a product to the cart, check out with your email and address, and pay with the Bogus Gateway (card number **1**, any future expiry, any CVC).\n4. In the admin, **fulfill** the new order (returns are only possible for fulfilled items).\n5. Log into the customer portal at https://<store>.myshopify.com/account (a one-time code is emailed to you), open the order and click **Request return** → fires **returns/request**.\n6. In the admin, open the order and **Approve** the return request → fires **returns/approve**.\n7. Optionally finish the journey in the admin: decline, cancel, close or reopen the return — each step fires its own event.\n\nThe trigger listens to the events selected in the **Return Events** property (all by default) and emits the fired topic in the `webhookTopic` output field. Note that `returns/update` alone never fires during a standard return journey — each step has its own topic.",
            "height": 380,
            "width": 380,
            "x": 64,
            "y": -100
        }
    }
}